# Singularity Rupture {3}{U}{B}{B}: "Destroy all creatures, then any number of target players each mill half their library, rounded down." Bot2's Dauthi Voidwalker exiles every card going to an
# opponent's graveyard instead (with a void counter), so Bot1's sacrificed Black Lotus is exiled, and its Memnite, destroyed together with the Voidwalker (CR 701.8a, 614), is too. Then Bot1 and Bot2,
# both targeted, each mill half of 23 cards, 11 (rounded down, CR 107.1a): Bot1's 11 go to its graveyard, with the Rupture, because the Voidwalker is gone by then. A creature is no target. The cost is
# {3}{U}{B}{B}, paid exactly with the Lotus's three B, the Sapphire's U and the Ruby and Pearl.

